WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:06.900
What if the stabby maniac was your best friend?&nbsp;
Or your ex-wife? What if it was you? These murder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.774
mysteries were all about the killer twist. And of&nbsp;
course we're talking spoilers for these movies.

00:00:12.774 --> 00:00:18.240
In 2021's "Last Night in Soho," Edgar&nbsp;
Wright teamed up with stars Anya Taylor-Joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.740
and Thomasin McKenzie to tell a twisted&nbsp;
tale of broken dreams and painful pasts.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.020
Ellie is an aspiring fashion student who&nbsp;
feels she belongs to the 1960s rather than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.800
present times. Ellie's wish appears to&nbsp;
come true when she gets transported in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.460
her dreams into the past. Ellie finds&nbsp;
herself sharing a body with Sandie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.600
an aspiring '60s singer who's&nbsp;
manipulated into forced sex work.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.260
After investigating, Ellie believes&nbsp;
Sandie was murdered by her pimp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.180
and she sets out to uncover the truth. In the end,&nbsp;
it's revealed that Sandie never died. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.540
she turned into a serial killer,&nbsp;
murdering the men who abused her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.031
and eventually became the landlady of the very&nbsp;
building where Ellie lives in the present day.

00:00:56.031 --> 00:01:02.460
"A girl did die up there&nbsp;
I supposed. The young me."

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.260
The "Murder on the Orient Express" stars its&nbsp;
director, Kenneth Branagh, in the lead role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.540
as one of the most famous fictional detectives,&nbsp;
Hercule Poirot. On board a lavish train in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:16.860
middle of nowhere, Poirot must grapple with an&nbsp;
unexpected murder that occurs during the journey.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.000
The venerated detective takes his time&nbsp;
examining the motives of each passenger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.020
on the train. He discovers that everyone&nbsp;
aboard has a past link to the victim and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:28.680
a plausible reason for wanting him&nbsp;
dead. So who was the killer? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.180
it's every single passenger on the train&nbsp;
except for Poirot. Turns out they'd all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.835
pooled their resources together and killed him as&nbsp;
a group to allay suspicion over any one person.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.240
In 2019's "Knives Out," filmmaker Rian Johnson&nbsp;
gave the world a new detective named Benoit Blanc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.100
a gentleman sleuth played by Daniel Craig&nbsp;
sporting an outrageous Southern accent.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.920
"That fateful night seems, at first glance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.180
to fill that hole perfectly. A&nbsp;
donut hole in a donut's hole."

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:01.320
The movie hinges on the murder of famed&nbsp;
novelist Harlan Thrombey and the many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.620
family members who stood to gain from&nbsp;
his death. Halfway through the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.700
another twist is thrown into the proceedings&nbsp;
when it's revealed that Harlan's death was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.080
a medical accident at the hands of his&nbsp;
nurse, Marta, played by Ana de Armas.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:17.820
But then it turns out a new mystery person&nbsp;
is blackmailing Marta in connection to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.800
murder. The only point of support for Marta is&nbsp;
Harlan's handsome and debonair grandson, Hugh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.540
played by Chris Evans. Marta's trust turns out&nbsp;
to be misplaced in the end when it's revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.860
that Hugh was the person who'd been secretly&nbsp;
blackmailing her, was also the killer of Harlan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.900
housekeeper, and set up the medical scenario&nbsp;
resulting in Harlan's death. The twists and turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:42.060
served up by "Knives Out" make it one of the most&nbsp;
entertaining entries in the murder mystery genre.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.687
Following the success of "The Da Vinci Code,"&nbsp;
the 2009 sequel "Angels and Demons," saw Tom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.687 --> 00:02:50.940
Hanks return as symbologist Robert&nbsp;
Langdon on a mission in the Vatican.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.200
The movie opens with the murder of&nbsp;
a reputed scientist and priest who'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.160
made a groundbreaking new scientific&nbsp;
discovery. The discovery led to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.600
creation of a bomb with massive destructive&nbsp;
capabilities. It falls to Langdon and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.660
allies to locate and dispose of&nbsp;
the weapon before it detonates.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.520
Among the people helping Langdon is Father&nbsp;
Patrick McKenna, played by Ewan McGregor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.500
the deceased pope's right-hand man. After coming&nbsp;
across as a messianic figure throughout the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.720
Langdon discovers near the end that McKenna&nbsp;
is responsible for the previous pope's death.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:27.180
In 2010, Martin Scorsese delivered a mind-bending&nbsp;
investigative thriller with "Shutter Island."

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:32.820
Set in the 1950s, the story takes place on a&nbsp;
lonely island that houses an institution for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.680
the mentally ill. Two U.S. marshals, Leonardo&nbsp;
DiCaprio's Teddy and Mark Ruffalo's Chuck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.640
arrive at the island to investigate&nbsp;
the disappearance of a woman. Teddy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.300
suspects it's somehow connected to a&nbsp;
missing patient named Andrew Laeddis.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.800
As Teddy draws closer to the heart of the mystery&nbsp;
surrounding the island and its inhabitants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.120
he comes to realize a shocking truth.&nbsp;
His real name is Andrew Laeddis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:59.040
and "Teddy the U.S. marshal" was an identity&nbsp;
he'd created to cope with the reality of having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.200
murdered his wife after she killed their three&nbsp;
children during a manic episode. Everything that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.860
"Teddy" sees and does throughout the movie&nbsp;
is his therapist's attempt to let him play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.660
out a fantasy and then return to the real&nbsp;
world after putting his delusions to rest.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:17.460
In the movie "Orphan" Kate and John Coleman&nbsp;
adopt a 9-year-old Russian girl named Esther&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:22.440
from a local orphanage. The arrangement seems&nbsp;
to work out well for a time ... until Esther&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.240
starts showcasing violent behavior and an&nbsp;
unusual degree of possessiveness towards John.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.980
After a series of tragic events befall&nbsp;
the family, all revolving around Esther,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.900
Kate discovers the truth of the matter.&nbsp;
Esther is in reality a 33-year-old woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.000
named Leena Klammer who suffers from a medical&nbsp;
condition that stunts her physical growth and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.840
keeps her looking unnaturally young.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Esther is plotting to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.633
Kate and her two other children out of the&nbsp;
way so she can have John all to herself.

00:04:50.633 --> 00:04:55.920
"The Invitation" follows Will, a man still&nbsp;
struggling with grief after a terrible tragedy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:01.260
To make things more complicated, he's attending&nbsp;
a dinner party being hosted by his ex-wife Eden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.940
and her new partner, David, complete with&nbsp;
friends he hasn't seen in years. Things are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.020
awkward from the get-go, and a bigger wrench&nbsp;
is thrown into the proceedings following the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.760
revelation that certain members of the party are&nbsp;
participants of a cult called "The Invitation."

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.560
It's later revealed that Eden and David are&nbsp;
acting on orders from the cult and intend to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:24.060
kill the other guests as a way to alleviate&nbsp;
all their pain and grief and move on to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:29.580
next plane of existence. Not only does the plan&nbsp;
work to a large extent, it's indicated at the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:34.769
that other members of the cult all over the city&nbsp;
are carrying out similar plans on a massive scale.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:40.440
The psychological horror film "Secret Window ''&nbsp;
follows Johnny Depp as mystery writer Mort Rainey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.400
whose life is crumbling around him&nbsp;
following a brutal divorce. Trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.960
escape his personal pain, Mort holes himself&nbsp;
away in a cabin for weeks to work in peace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.160
although he struggles to write. That's when&nbsp;
a man named Shooter arrives to confront&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.580
Mort over claims that the author&nbsp;
plagiarized Shooter's short story.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.260
As everything falls into place in the film's&nbsp;
finale, it's revealed that Mort suffers from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:06.300
mental disorder, and he created the alternate&nbsp;
personality of "Shooter" as a way to cope. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.200
was always Mort's intention, acting as&nbsp;
Shooter, to kill his ex-wife and her new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:15.420
husband. He succeeds in doing so by the end&nbsp;
of the film and happily goes back to work.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:20.580
In "Primal Fear" Richard Gere plays Martin&nbsp;
Vail, a hotshot defense attorney obsessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:25.080
with money and fame. However, Vail is attracted&nbsp;
to the case of the murder of an archbishop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:29.760
with the chief suspect being 19-year-old&nbsp;
altar boy Aaron Stampler, played by Edward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:34.200
Norton. The court case becomes a matter of&nbsp;
convincing the jury that meek little Aaron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.500
with his stutter and his violent&nbsp;
split personality of "Roy," was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.640
not in his right mind when he killed the&nbsp;
archbishop, a man he loved and admired.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:46.260
After a hard-fought battle, Vail wins his&nbsp;
case and gets Aaron acquitted using the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:51.060
insanity plea. In one of the most shocking&nbsp;
twists in cinema history, Aaron reveals to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.720
Vail at the end that he'd been acting the&nbsp;
whole time. He had in fact been responsible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:59.520
for killing the archbishop in cold blood, and&nbsp;
"Roy" was his true personality the whole time.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:04.320
"There never was an Aaron, counselor."

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:13.860
The original "Saw" in 2004 pretty much became&nbsp;
the poster child for "hiding the killer in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:18.720
plain sight." The breakout success of that film&nbsp;
meant a sequel was released only a year later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:24.360
and the twist this time was…well, it used the&nbsp;
same twist. In "Saw 2," a new batch of victims are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:29.880
imprisoned by Jigsaw, including Amanda Young, a&nbsp;
woman he'd captured once before. The group is then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.200
made to solve a series of bloody and horrifying&nbsp;
"escape rooms" with the promise of a painful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.940
death if they fail to follow the instructions&nbsp;
or try to cheat. You know the story by now.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:44.100
After playing the game almost to the end,&nbsp;
Detective Matthew's son, Daniel, appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:48.720
to be one of the last players standing. Daniel&nbsp;
was targeted because Matthews was a corrupt cop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.640
who's ruined many lives by planting false&nbsp;
evidence. This leads the detective to race&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:59.160
towards Daniel's location only to be captured, and&nbsp;
it's revealed that Amanda has become an accomplice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:03.720
of Jigsaw's.She'd been working alongside&nbsp;
the killer the whole time, and in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:09.202
she leaves Matthews to die alone in a room while&nbsp;
Jigsaw watches the whole thing with satisfaction.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:13.320
In the film "Gothika," Halle Berry&nbsp;
plays the role of Dr. Miranda Grey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:18.420
a psychiatrist who suffers a car crash one night.&nbsp;
Waking up in the penitentiary where she works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:21.540
Miranda is shocked to find out that she's&nbsp;
been charged with killing her husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.360
although she can't recall the&nbsp;
events of the day he died.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:28.500
As Miranda travels deeper down the road to&nbsp;
solving the mystery of her incarceration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.880
it's revealed that her late husband had&nbsp;
been a serial killer. To make matters worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.620
Miranda also realizes at the last moment that&nbsp;
Sheriff Bob Ryan, who seemed to be helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.300
clear her name, was actually her late husband's&nbsp;
accomplice who planned to kill her off as well.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.580
The movie "Scream" follows Sidney Prescott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:48.240
who's friends are being targeted by the&nbsp;
masked Ghostface killer who likes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:52.620
make taunting phone calls to his victims before&nbsp;
attacking them in their most vulnerable moment.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.340
As the plot unfolds, Sidney becomes&nbsp;
convinced that her boyfriend, Billy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.300
is the killer. But getting him jailed still&nbsp;
doesn't stop the killer from finding another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.440
victim. Things come to a head during the third&nbsp;
act of the movie when Billy's best friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:09.120
Stu Macher, throws a party to celebrate&nbsp;
the early closure of their school. Amidst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.660
fresh murders at the party, Sidney&nbsp;
finally learns that both Billy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:17.424
Stu took turns becoming Ghostface to avoid&nbsp;
suspicion falling on either one of them.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.360
One of Christopher Nolan's earlier films,&nbsp;
"Memento," is one of the best thrillers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:25.920
in Hollywood history. The film opens with Guy&nbsp;
Pearce's Leonard Shelby, a man suffering from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:31.260
anterograde amnesia, which means that he forgets&nbsp;
new memories after 15 minutes. What caused the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:36.180
amnesia? According to Leonard, two thugs broke&nbsp;
into his home, assaulted him, and killed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:40.500
beloved wife. However, the cops don't believe&nbsp;
there were two criminals involved in the crime.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:45.720
So Leonard embarks on a solo crusade to bring&nbsp;
the second thug to justice, whose name Leonard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:50.400
believes to be "John G." After finally tracking&nbsp;
down and killing the man he thinks to be John G,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:55.080
Leonard learns the startling truth. He'd already&nbsp;
killed the person he was after a year ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.800
and he's been killing different men since&nbsp;
then to keep up his confused crusade.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.940
"Come on, you got your revenge.&nbsp;
Enjoy it while you still remember."

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:08.340
The 1960 psychological horror thriller classic&nbsp;
"Psycho" opens with a woman named Marion Crane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:12.120
on the run from the law in connection with&nbsp;
a crime. Looking for shelter for the night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:18.540
Marion stops at the nondescript Bates Motel run&nbsp;
by a timid and nervy manager Norman Bates, a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:23.460
who resides in a house near the motel along with&nbsp;
his angry, abusive mother. That night, Marion is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:28.200
violently killed by a woman thought to be Norman's&nbsp;
mom suffering from some sort of criminal mania.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:33.120
Marion's disappearance at the motel attracts&nbsp;
the attention of her sister, Lila, and local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:38.100
authorities. Lila conducts her own search that&nbsp;
yields the mummified corpse of Norman's mother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.840
It's then revealed that Norman had killed his&nbsp;
mother many years ago and developed a split&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.700
personality that prompted him to dress up like&nbsp;
her and kill any woman he became attracted to.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:53.640
2003's neo-noir slasher "Identity" follows&nbsp;
10 random travelers that are drawn to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:57.660
deserted motel one night to escape a&nbsp;
rainstorm. Over the night, one by one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:02.460
each of the travelers are killed off. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
in a different location, Malcolm Rivers has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:06.480
accused of committing a mass murder, and the&nbsp;
only way to get him acquitted is with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.980
help of a journal that may contain major clues&nbsp;
regarding the truth about what really went down.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:16.020
Amid a lot of twists and turns, it's revealed&nbsp;
that all the characters at the motel are split&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:21.600
personalities belonging to Malcolm's fractured&nbsp;
psyche. The purpose of imagining the motel is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:26.220
way to help Malcolm kill off one particular&nbsp;
alternate personality, which is a murderous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:30.780
psychopath. While Malcolm succeeds in killing&nbsp;
off the personality he thinks is the killer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:34.560
it's eventually revealed that the real&nbsp;
threat all along had been "Timmy," a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.880
10-year-old personality that had actually&nbsp;
been responsible for the carnage at the hotel.

